From 7e23760a56503062455c2b8ce8ee5583201f2133 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CharlieChen114514 <725610365@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 10:50:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] uboot: evb-rk3506 SD autoboot via CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND (mmc
 read + bootm)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Sibling of the NAND autoboot (0003): a separate defconfig that autoboots from
the SD card instead of NAND. Identical to evb-rk3506_defconfig EXCEPT the
compiled-default bootcmd loads the SD kernel FIT via `mmc read` (raw, sector
0x4000) instead of `mtd read`, and bootargs set root=/dev/mmcblk0p3 (the SD GPT
p3 ext4 — 3 partitions: uboot=p1, boot=p2, rootfs=p3) so the kernel mounts the
SD ext4 root, not NAND UBIFS.

env=nowhere runs the compiled-default bootcmd every boot, so the SD card boots
to a shell with zero manual input (SD-2). SD-1 needed hand-typed mmc read at the
=> prompt. Load offset 0x4000 + read length 0x5000 match the verified manual
sequence (log boot-sdl-202606211028); the mmc@ff480000 DT node is from 0004.

The NAND defconfig is UNCHANGED — the NAND update.img keeps its mtd-read bootcmd.
The two defconfigs produce two uboot images (uboot.img / uboot-sd.img), selected
by the build-uboot/pack-fit/assemble --variant sd chain (forge stage_pack_sd).
---
 configs/evb-rk3506_sd_defconfig | 63 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 63 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 configs/evb-rk3506_sd_defconfig

diff --git a/configs/evb-rk3506_sd_defconfig b/configs/evb-rk3506_sd_defconfig
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..36eac90a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/configs/evb-rk3506_sd_defconfig
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+CONFIG_ARM=y
+CONFIG_SKIP_LOWLEVEL_INIT=y
+CONFIG_COUNTER_FREQUENCY=24000000
+CONFIG_ARCH_ROCKCHIP=y
+CONFIG_DEFAULT_DEVICE_TREE="rk3506-evb"
+CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_RK3506=y
+CONFIG_SYS_LOAD_ADDR=0xc00800
+CONFIG_DEBUG_UART_BASE=0xff0a0000
+CONFIG_DEBUG_UART_CLOCK=24000000
+CONFIG_DEBUG_UART=y
+# CONFIG_BOOTMETH_VBE is not set
+CONFIG_DEFAULT_FDT_FILE="rockchip/rk3506-evb.dtb"
+# CONFIG_DISPLAY_CPUINFO is not set
+CONFIG_SPL_MAX_SIZE=0x40000
+# CONFIG_SPL_RAW_IMAGE_SUPPORT is not set
+CONFIG_SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_SECTOR=0x2000
+CONFIG_CMD_MEMINFO=y
+CONFIG_CMD_MEMINFO_MAP=y
+CONFIG_CMD_GPIO=y
+CONFIG_CMD_GPT=y
+CONFIG_CMD_MISC=y
+CONFIG_CMD_MMC=y
+# CONFIG_CMD_SETEXPR is not set
+CONFIG_CMD_RNG=y
+# CONFIG_SPL_DOS_PARTITION is not set
+# CONFIG_OF_UPSTREAM is not set
+# CONFIG_TOOLS_MKEFICAPSULE is not set
+CONFIG_OF_SPL_REMOVE_PROPS="clock-names interrupt-parent assigned-clocks assigned-clock-rates assigned-clock-parents"
+CONFIG_NO_NET=y
+# CONFIG_ADC is not set
+CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_GPIO=y
+CONFIG_MMC_DW=y
+CONFIG_MMC_DW_ROCKCHIP=y
+CONFIG_BAUDRATE=1500000
+CONFIG_DEBUG_UART_SHIFT=2
+CONFIG_SYS_NS16550_MEM32=y
+CONFIG_ERRNO_STR=y
+
+# SPI SFC controller + SPI NAND (Winbond W25N04KV, 512MB) — kept for parity with
+# the NAND defconfig; the SD bootcmd below ignores NAND (SD boot doesn't touch it).
+CONFIG_DM_SPI=y
+CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_SFC=y
+CONFIG_MTD=y
+CONFIG_DM_MTD=y
+CONFIG_MTD_SPI_NAND=y
+CONFIG_CMD_MTD=y
+# kernel boot
+CONFIG_FIT=y
+CONFIG_CMD_BOOTM=y
+CONFIG_CMD_BOOTZ=y
+CONFIG_SYS_BOOTM_LEN=0x2000000
+# NAND partition: boot = 16MB @ sector 0xBA00 (= byte 0x1740000), holds kernel FIT
+CONFIG_MTDPARTS_DEFAULT="mtdparts=spi-nand0:16m@0x1740000(boot)"
+
+# autoboot (SD): env=nowhere → compiled-default bootcmd runs every boot. Loads the
+# SD kernel FIT (boot.img @ sector 0x4000) via `mmc read` (RAW, no fs: defconfig has
+# CMD_MMC but no ext4/FAT/load — same raw philosophy as NAND's mtd read), then
+# bootm. rootfs = the SD GPT p3 ext4 (root=/dev/mmcblk0p3 — 3 partitions: uboot=p1,
+# boot=p2, rootfs=p3; NOT p1 like the raw dd image). Board-verified manual sequence
+# (boot-sdl-202606211028); this bakes it into CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND → SD-2 autoboot.
+# The NAND defconfig is UNCHANGED (its mtd-read bootcmd); this is a sibling image.
+CONFIG_USE_BOOTCOMMAND=y
+CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND="setenv bootargs 'console=ttyS0,1500000 root=/dev/mmcblk0p3 rootwait rw'; mmc dev 0; mmc read 0x04000000 0x4000 0x5000; bootm 0x04000000"
-- 
